      "title": "Citigroup: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors",
      "summary": "Citigroup reported Q3 2026 net income of $5.2 billion, with management executing a structural overhaul that cuts costs through severance-funded headcount reductions while reinvesting in AI and technology. The bank reduced tech vendor spending by 30% year-over-year through internal AI deployment, and wealth management attracted $38 billion in net new investment assets, doubling year-over-year. Revenue expanded 8% as the bank pursues disciplined expense controls and balance sheet allocation toward long-term financial targets.",
