      "title": "JPMorgan vs. Citigroup: Which Stock Has the Edge After Q3 Results?",
      "summary": "JPMorgan and Citigroup reported Q3 earnings with contrasting profiles. JPMorgan demonstrated earnings resilience with 6% net income growth, benefiting from higher net interest income and loan growth, while maintaining industry-leading profitability and a strong balance sheet. Citigroup delivered robust 40% net income growth as its multiyear restructuring gains momentum, with improved efficiency ratios and cost discipline. JPMorgan trades at a premium valuation (13.41X forward P/E) reflecting its stability, while Citigroup's discounted valuation (9.74X) presents greater upside potential if its turnaround succeeds. Both stocks carry a Zacks Rank #3 (Hold) rating.",
